# Mosquitto ACL - carPosTracking.
#
# Nothing is permitted unless it is granted below: a topic with no matching rule
# for that user is denied, and anonymous clients are refused at connect time
# (allow_anonymous false in mosquitto.conf). There are deliberately no rules
# outside a `user` block - such rules would apply to every client, which is
# exactly the unauthorized access this file exists to prevent.
#
# Mosquitto also needs an explicit `read` rule for a topic before it will DELIVER
# a message to a subscriber. Without one it still ACKs the SUBSCRIBE and then
# silently drops every message, which looks exactly like a broken broker. If a
# client connects and subscribes fine but never receives anything, the missing
# rule is almost always here.
#
# Usernames below are literal and must match the *_USER values in .env.

# admin: full access, including $SYS for manual debugging.
user admin
topic readwrite #
topic read $SYS/#

# GNSS01: the tracker. Publishes its fixes, reads only its own command topic.
user GNSS01
topic write devices/GNSS01
topic read devices/GNSS01/cmd

# dashboard: consumes every device's fixes and sends commands back.
user dashboard
topic read devices/#
topic write devices/+/cmd

# healthcheck: the container's own liveness probe, and nothing else. It is scoped
# to a single throwaway topic on purpose - the probe never needs to see device
# data, so a leak of these credentials exposes nothing.
user healthcheck
topic readwrite healthcheck/probe
